<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Telerj H1 net falls vs yr ago.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Telerj H1 net falls vs yr ago.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Telerj, a unit of federal telecom  holding Telebras serving Rio de Janeiro state, released the following  January-June 1997 financial results.</p>
<p>		Jan-June 1997	    Jan-June 1996</p>
<p>Net	     46.13 million	    53.39 million</p>
<p>Shr Net	 1.76			 2.04</p>
<p>Net Revs	674.7 million	    591.9 million</p>
<p>Gross Revs    879.8 million	    791.9 million</p>
<p>Oper Net	68.16 million	    80.07 million</p>
<p>Net Worth     2.636 billion	    2.568 billion</p>
<p>Note: Figures are in Brazilian reais and not adjusted for inflation.  Share net is per lot of 1,000 shares.</p>
<p>The company, formally named Telecomunicacoes do Rio de Janeiro SA,  reported 1.907 million fixed lines installed and 186,000 cellular  terminals in service in the first-half compared with 1.843 million  fixed lines and 167,000 cellular terminals at the end of December  1996.</p>
<p>((-- James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485413))</p>
